  'settings.appLock.backupNote': 'To turn the app PIN or passphrase on, first type two words of your recovery phrase from your written backup, to confirm you still have it.',
  'settings.appLock.strength': 'How hard each is to guess from a copy of this app\'s files: a 6-digit PIN is one of a million (about 20 bits), which one computer can try in about 3 days. Four random words picked with dice are about 52 bits, millions of years for the same computer. A sentence you make up may be much easier to guess than its length suggests: the 15-character minimum cannot measure that.',
  'settings.appLock.passphraseAdvice': 'A passphrase is typed on your keyboard each time the wallet opens. Use four or more random words, for example picked with dice, not a sentence or quotation someone could guess. Do not use words from your recovery phrase. Do not save it in a password manager: this wallet turns autofill off for it.',
  'settings.appLock.keyboardNote': 'Unlike the PIN pad, your keyboard sees what you type. Use a keyboard you trust.',
