  'settings.appPin.switch': 'Use a passphrase instead',
  'settings.duress.pin.title': 'Duress PIN',
  'settings.duress.pin.explanation': 'A duress PIN opens a separate wallet instead of this one, for when someone forces you to open your wallet. Keep a small amount in it and use it now and then so it looks lived in.',
  'settings.duress.pin.claim': 'The duress PIN opens a separate wallet instead of this one, so someone looking at the screen sees an ordinary wallet. Anyone who copies this app\'s files from the phone can tell that two wallets exist, and a 6-digit PIN can be guessed from such a copy. Funding the second wallet from this wallet links them on-chain.',
  'settings.duress.pin.backup': 'The second wallet is derived from this wallet\'s recovery phrase (BIP-85, child index 0), so backing up that one phrase backs up both: restoring this phrase and setting a duress PIN again brings the same second wallet back. Its own recovery phrase does not reveal this wallet\'s: someone shown it learns nothing of this wallet.',
