  'recordsBackup.restore': 'Restore',
  'recordsBackup.confirmTitle': 'Restore records from this backup?',
  'recordsBackup.what': 'A records backup is one file with the records this wallet keeps on this phone: contacts, transaction notes, networks you added, tracked tokens, guardian recovery records, multi-signature account records, bridge transfers, price alerts and spending limits. It contains no private key, no recovery phrase and no PIN.',
  'recordsBackup.key': 'The file is encrypted with a key made from this wallet’s recovery phrase, so only this recovery phrase can open it — on this phone, or on another phone after you restore the phrase there. If you lose the recovery phrase, this backup is lost with it.',
  'recordsBackup.notIncluded': 'Not in the backup and not restored by it: session keys (they never leave this phone; a payment, subscription or recurring swap must be revoked and set up again), imported private keys (only the copy of the key you kept yourself can restore such an account) and passkeys (the phone’s passkey provider holds them, not this wallet). Account names, watched addresses, connected apps, pending transactions and spending history are not included either.',
  'recordsBackup.merge': 'Restoring adds only the records that are not on this phone yet. A record that is already here — the same contact address, note, network, token, account, transfer, alert or limit — is kept exactly as it is and never overwritten. Each record is checked as when it was first saved, and a network you added is checked again through its RPC address. A multi-signature account comes back without its operation history.',
